OL,3,GNEWSADeath of pony in 'blind panic'
OL,4,Asparks dog warning
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe owner of a New Forest pony has said
OL,7,Fher horse was sent into a "blind panic"
OL,8,Fafter apparently being chased by a
OL,9,Floose dog.
OL,11,FHonor Dovey-Humble said her
OL,12,Ffive-year-old mare, Bessie, was found
OL,13,Fseverely injured near Beaulieu early on
OL,14,FThursday and had to be put down the
OL,15,Fnext day.
OL,17,FThe horse's leg was broken, seemingly
OL,18,Fthe result of slipping or falling after
OL,19,Frunning from the dog. Horses were
OL,20,Freported stampeding near Beaulieu the
OL,21,Fprevious evening.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,337,330,200,160,0,100
